Description: Choose the ports of the tests' HTTP endpoints below the range of local ports of outgoing connections.
 The tests listen with HTTP endpoints on random ports from 30000 to 65000 and on the fixed ports 54321 to 54323,
 mostly within the range from which Linux chooses the local ports of outgoing connections, 32768 to 60999. The tests'
 own HTTP connections to their endpoints keep the local port of their client side in TIME_WAIT for a minute after they
 close, up to 71 ports at once during one run of the suite, and an endpoint cannot listen on a port which such a
 connection still occupies. A test then failed with "Address already in use", or waited until meson killed it when it
 waited for an endpoint which never started, as tracker-serialize-test did and the functional tests do, which failed
 builds of the package. The random ports are now from 10000 to 31999 and the fixed ones 32321 to 32323, below that
 range on Linux and below the ranges other systems use for outgoing connections.
Author: Mitar
Forwarded: no
Last-Update: 2026-11-27
